WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.680
Good morning John!

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.740
Thanks for the update on America's healthcare situation.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.920
Something tells me that this isn't going to be the last video where you talk about that.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.399
For people who aren't in America,

00:00:07.399 --> 00:00:10.139
sorry it's a really big deal for us right
now.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.460
Sometimes I'm really surprised by what people of the world wanna see and,

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.830
of course, sometimes you wanna see silly videos,

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.300
sometimes you wanna see complicated videos
where we explain things

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.600
and one of the things that really surprised me: when we did the Nerdfighter survey

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.900
a huge majority of people said that
they wished I would spend more time

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.960
writing and producing and releasing songs.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.140
So this is really dumb, this is like textbook example my brain being broken.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:36.060
When I release a Vlogbrothers video I look at the number of likes and dislikes that the video gets.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.360
Average, we get about 12,000 likes and about 100 dislikes.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.620
When I put up a song, and this is going to sound really dumb,

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.160
the number of dislikes will be like double the usual.

00:00:45.169 --> 00:00:52.209
That's still only 200 people of 200,000 people disliking the video.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.879
But because it's more than usual, my
brain says

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.740
that's not as good as the normal video
so stop doing those.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:05.740
For so long I pushed making new music to the back burner because I felt like it wasn't as

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.820
successful as the other kinds of videos we made.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.800
So yeah, after I got the survey results that lots of people wanted me to make more music,

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.000
I started making more music.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.140
For example, I just wrote a song called 'Undigested Lump',

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:19.009
which is about being super angry at
someone and insulting them using only

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:21.799
Shakespearean insults and I'm going to
play it for you right now.

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:24.869
Well I got lot of things I'd like
to say to you

00:01:24.869 --> 00:01:30.171
and also just a few I like to actually
do but I don't wanna go to jail and

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:34.660
sometimes my words fail and I don't want to let the worst parts in me prevail.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.939
Saying what's on my mind for me has
always been hard so I'm just gonna leave

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.280
this to the words of the Bard: Get out of my sight! Thou dost infect my eyes.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:46.540
Wilt thou be made a man out of my vice?

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.400
O braggart vile and damned furious wight!

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.700
Thy tongue outvenoms all the worms of Nile.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.520
Oh hell must be empty 'cause the devil is here.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:00.160
I've been memorising Shakespeare for nine years.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.000
So I was ready for this.

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:06.500
After what you did, you'll be lucky if
you leave here and you still exist.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.900
You never knew when to shut it.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.620
You carcass fit for hounds.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.440
It's the emptiest vessel that makes the loudest sounds.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.380
Get out of my sight! Thou dost infect my eyes.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:17.940
Wilt thou be made a man out of my vice?

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.900
O braggart vile and damned furious wight!

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.960
Thy tongue outvenoms all the worms of Nile.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.880
Injurious, tedious, you bought yourself prentice.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.300
Remorseless, trecherous, lecherous stock fish.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.800
Thou one-trunk-inheriting slave.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:39.440
You are not worth another word, or else I'd call you, I'd call you a knave.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:43.820
So you might notice that was a little short, I cut one of the verses off cause it's got a little bit dirty.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:47.540
Also, this video wouldn't have fit into a four minute video if I had left the verse on.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:53.420
So... Vlogbrothers rules. I'll be working on an album in November and October.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.500
A bunch of my favourite YouTube musicians are gonna be helping me.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.420
Also probably some of my favourite wizard rock musicians.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.480
It's gonna be maybe a different level from my other albums.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:06.060
Not to say that my other albums aren't great. I'm pointing at them. They're right over there on that shelf.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.120
I wanted to a be a little more musically cohesive, energetic, but not so weirdly genre isolated with

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.860
like, punk rock next to polka. Not that there's anything wrong with that.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:20.940
Instead, I wanna like, mash and like, have some flow so it's punk rock polka instead of punk rock, polka.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:24.180
God, now I have to put a punk rock polka song on that album. Oh well.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.820
Nerdfighteria, thank you for supporting me and something in something that I really love doing.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:33.900
I'm sorry that I was being dumb about it, and yay! Now more music! I punched my microphone. Calm down son.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.060
